# Recipe search diagnostics - issue #288
# Suggested repository location: api/src/RestClient/10-search.rest
#
# Uses the same REST Client environment variables as the existing .rest files:
#   baseUrl        API origin, e.g. http://localhost:5050 (no trailing /api).
#   hearthSecret   Your existing local REST Client secret. Never commit it.
#   familyMemberId Your existing REST Client family member ID.
# Select your usual REST Client environment before sending requests.
# No real credentials are included. No requests were executed to prepare this file.
#
# Run each request individually. The first six are controlled comparisons:
# same limit, empty hard filters, no planner/similar context or continuation.
# Typed poultry/chicken/fish use query. Poultry/Fish chips use
# preferences.concepts, NOT filters.categories or filters.includedIngredients.
# Fetch vocabulary first: deployments can configure a different concept for an ID.
# If so, replace poultry/fish in the CHIP request bodies with returned main[].concept.
#
# Inspect the unwrapped JSON response:
#   topPick and results: count BOTH; limit counts alternatives, not topPick.
#   appliedFilters: hard filters only; does not echo preferences.concepts.
#   searchMode: discovery for the empty probe and explicit for constrained probes.
#   resultPath: browse, lexical-only, hybrid, fallback-lexical,
#               or semantic-only (emitted by current implementation for chips).
#   results[].id/name/score/reasons and topPick.id/name/score/reasons.
#   nextCursor: more results, not proof the first page contains every match.
# A successful semantic-only zero-match is not retried lexically by the service.
# Concept-only fallback uses the selected concept text.
# The current OpenAPI resultPath enum omits semantic-only (and similar);
# preserve the actual response value rather than treating it as invalid.
#
# For UI parity, copy its active filters, preferences and optional weekOffset,
# dayIndex, similarToRecipeId into the request; keep them identical across comparisons.
# Baseline search includes ready, non-soft-deleted recipes; it does not default
# to discoverableOnly. Do not infer missing recipes from an empty first page alone.
# 401: check environment/auth. 400: check JSON and limit (1..50).
# 409: restart first page without continuationToken.
# 503: recovery is busy; respect Retry-After.
#
# Source-checked against main commit e84a2d786d900b7757b43a0bf61606ba249be442 (2026-10-20 UTC).
# No repository writes, deployments, reindexing, or production requests performed.
